---
const steps = [
  "Scan files",
  "Analyze files",
  "Build the dependency graph",
  "Detect the framework",
  "Detect routes",
  "Detect the database",
  "Extract entities",
  "Detect capabilities",
  "Detect features",
  "Infer the domain",
  "Rank critical files",
  "Generate flows"
];
const optionalAi = "Infer the domain";

const facts = [
  { value: "12", label: "pipeline steps" },
  { value: "3", label: "optional AI calls" },
  { value: "0", label: "keys needed to analyze" }
];
---

<section class="method section page" aria-labelledby="method-title">
  <div class="method__intro" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow__dot"></span>Method</p>
    <h2 class="section__title method__title" id="method-title">
      The same code gives the same map.
    </h2>
    <p class="method__copy">
      Files, imports, routes, features and flows come from static analysis, so
      the result doesn't change between runs. AI is optional and is used in
      three places: inferring what the project is for, describing files, and
      answering questions. If the provider fails, <code>devmap analyze</code>{" "}
      still finishes.
    </p>

    <dl class="method__facts">
      {facts.map((fact) => (
        <div>
          <dt>{fact.value}</dt>
          <dd>{fact.label}</dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>
  </div>

  <ol class="method__steps card" aria-label="What devmap analyze does, in order" data-reveal style="--i:2">
    {steps.map((step) => (
      <li>
        <span class="method__label">{step}</span>
        {step === optionalAi && <span class="method__ai">optional AI</span>}
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>
</section>

<style>
  .method {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
    align-items: start;
  }

  @media (min-width: 62rem) {
    .method {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 6fr) minmax(0, 5fr);
    }
  }

  .method__intro {
    display: grid;
    justify-items: start;
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 62rem) {
    .method__intro {
      position: sticky;
      top: calc(var(--sticky-offset) + 1.5rem);
    }
  }

  .method__title {
    max-width: 10em;
  }

  .method__copy {
    max-width: 34rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .method__copy code {
    font-size: 0.875em;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .method__facts {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, auto));
    gap: 1.5rem clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    padding-top: 1.75rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 32rem;
  }

  .method__facts dt {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .method__facts dd {
    margin: 0.4rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .method__steps {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0.6rem 1.5rem;
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: step;
  }

  .method__steps li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding-block: 0.85rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    color: var(--ink);
    counter-increment: step;
  }

  .method__steps li:last-child {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  .method__steps li::before {
    content: counter(step, decimal-leading-zero);
    flex: none;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 2rem;
    height: 2rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .method__label {
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .method__ai {
    margin-left: auto;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.6rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--accent-wash);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    white-space: nowrap;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
